  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "What services do you offer?",
      "tag": "Services",
      "answer": "I design book interiors, covers, journals, planners, workbooks, and ebooks. Most projects combine several of these, so the cover and the pages inside share one consistent look.",
      "order": 0
    },
    {
      "question": "What is your typical turnaround time?",
      "tag": "Timeline",
      "answer": "A cover usually takes one to two weeks. A full interior takes three to six weeks, depending on the page count and how complex the layout is. You get a clear schedule before we start.",
      "order": 1
    },
    {
      "question": "Which files will I receive?",
      "tag": "Files",
      "answer": "You receive print-ready PDFs with the correct bleed and trim for your printer, plus an EPUB or interactive PDF if your project includes a digital edition. Source files are available on request.",
      "order": 2
    },
    {
      "question": "Can you prepare files for Amazon KDP or IngramSpark?",
      "tag": "Printing",
      "answer": "Yes. I set up the trim size, margins, bleed, and spine width to match your printer's specifications, so the files pass their checks on the first upload.",
      "order": 3
    },
    {
      "question": "How many revisions are included?",
      "tag": "Revisions",
      "answer": "Each project includes two rounds of revisions at every main stage: concept, layout, and final files. Extra rounds can be added if needed.",
      "order": 4
    },
    {
      "question": "What does your process look like?",
      "tag": "Process",
      "answer": "We start with a short brief about your book and readers. Then I present a design direction, build the layout, refine it with your feedback, and deliver final files ready for print and digital use.",
      "order": 5
    }
  ],
